{"timestamp":"2026-09-02T16:34:11.961673Z","level":"info","event":"    \"summary_description\": \"The U.S. Department of State Bureau of Democracy, Human Rights, and Labor (DRL) seeks to\\u202fmake available on-demand, emergency support for individuals and organizations that face imminent threat due to their work to\\u202fpromote and defend\\u202ffundamental freedoms, including the freedoms of speech, peaceful assembly, and association articulated in the United States\\u2019 founding documents. The program will provide assistance to defenders\\u202fwho are\\u202ffacing\\u202fthreat of attack, arbitrary arrest, detention, prosecution, or\\u202fare\\u202fotherwise at imminent risk of harm, through a program that provides short-term emergency funding to enable them to continue their\\u202fwork pressing for democratic government and reform and respect for human rights.\",","logger":"task.stdout"}
